    [36mdueDate[39m: [31m"2026-10-01"[39m | [34mnull[39m, [32m// date-only ISO string, no time, no timezone[39m
    [36mcreatedAt[39m: [31m"2026-09-16T14:22:31.004Z"[39m,
    [36mupdatedAt[39m: [31m"2026-09-16T14:22:31.004Z"[39m
  }

  [38;5;153mdueDate[39m is deliberately date-only. "Due Oct 1" means the whole day in the user's local timezone; storing an instant
  would make a task shift days when travelling, and the notification layer would inherit that bug.

  [1mChange event[0m

  {
    [36mid[39m: [31m"e_..."[39m,
    [36mtype[39m: [31m"task.created"[39m | [31m"task.updated"[39m | [31m"task.completed"[39m | [31m"task.reopened"[39m | [31m"task.deleted"[39m,
    [36mtaskId[39m: [31m"t_..."[39m,
    [36mat[39m: [31m"2026-09-16T14:22:31.004Z"[39m,
    [36mactor[39m: [31m"local"[39m,                       [32m// the seam: a server fills in a user id later[39m
    [36mtitle[39m: [31m"Renew passport"[39m,              [32m// snapshot, so deleted tasks still read sensibly[39m
    [36mchanges[39m: { [36mdueDate[39m: { [36mfrom[39m: [34mnull[39m, [36mto[39m: [31m"2026-10-01"[39m } }  [32m// updated only[39m
  }

  Three decisions worth surfacing:

  - [1m[38;5;153mcompleted[39m/[38;5;153mreopened[39m are their own types[0m, not [38;5;153mupdated[39m with a [38;5;153mdone[39m field. Completion is the event a notification layer
    most wants to speak about, and special-casing it in every consumer is worse than naming it once here.
  - [1m[38;5;153mactor[39m exists from day one[0m and is always [38;5;153m"local"[39m. It's one field now and it's the difference between "a task changed"
    and "Sam changed a task" later.
  - [1mThe event snapshots [38;5;153mtitle[39m.[0m Without it, a notification about a deleted task can only say "a task was deleted" — the
    log has to stand alone.

  [1mPersistence:[0m three [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m keys — [38;5;153mtasks.v1[39m, [38;5;153mevents.v1[39m, [38;5;153mschema.v1[39m (holding [38;5;153m{version: 1}[39m). The version key is what
  lets a future change migrate rather than guess.

  Does the data model look right before I move to data flow and testing?

